    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d633">

                <pb facs="0673" n="661" xml:id="pg661"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/8926: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-03-10T19:00:00+02:00">March 10, 1941—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 10—3:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>344. My 327, March 7, 6 p.m., and 300, March 3, 5 p.m.<anchor n="44"
                        xml:id="d633-f1"/> From same reliable source I am informed Mussolini is now
                    in Albania and insists upon proceeding with counter-offensive against Greeks. He
                    is determined at least to begin without assistance of Germans. I am also
                    informed that offensive may be undertaken at end of this week.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
